<title>FRANCE: Air Liquide H1 sales rise 11 pct.</title>
<headline>Air Liquide H1 sales rise 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>     Turnover				 18,491  vs  16,657</p>
<p>	- gases				 13,512  vs  11,956</p>
<p>	- welding				2,064  vs   1,894</p>
<p>	- engineering &amp; construction	 649  vs     889</p>
<p>	- chemistry and sundry	     2,266  vs   1,918</p>
<p>NOTE - Air Liquide said sales rose 11.0 percent, with a positive foreign exchange impact of 3.9 percent. The US dollar conversion rate was 5.69 francs for the first half of 1997, compared with 5.10 francs a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The first half year of 1997 confirms the improvement of the business activity since the end of the year 1996, reinforced by contracts coming on stream resulting from commercial successes obtained by the group in 1995 and 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
